WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.273
The next day, Heidi made a suggestion:

2
00:00:03.274 --> 00:00:10.086
"Clara, I can read aloud to you every day, just as I did for Grandmamma."

3
00:00:10.087 --> 00:00:15.604
Clara agreed, and Heidi started reading with her usual enthusiasm.

4
00:00:15.605 --> 00:00:18.731
But Heidi had hardly begun when she cried out,

5
00:00:18.732 --> 00:00:23.862
"Oh no! Then Grannie is dead!" and burst into tears.

6
00:00:23.863 --> 00:00:26.905
The story was about a dying grandmother.

7
00:00:26.906 --> 00:00:35.797
It seemed so real to her that Heidi could not stop thinking that it was Peter's grandmother who had died.

8
00:00:35.798 --> 00:00:37.478
"She is dead.

9
00:00:37.479 --> 00:00:40.272
I shall never see her again.

10
00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:45.828
She never had the chance to eat one white roll," Heidi sobbed.

11
00:00:45.829 --> 00:00:51.021
Clara explained over and over that the story was about a different grandmother.

12
00:00:51.022 --> 00:00:58.427
But even when Heidi understood that it was only a story and not real, she couldn't stop weeping.

13
00:00:58.428 --> 00:01:02.827
Fraulein came into the room and Clara explained what had happened.

14
00:01:02.828 --> 00:01:07.208
As Heidi continued to weep, Fraulein became impatient.

15
00:01:07.209 --> 00:01:11.997
"Now, Heidi, that is enough!" she said.

16
00:01:11.998 --> 00:01:20.179
"If you act like this again while you are reading, I will take your book away and never let you have it again!"

17
00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.268
Fraulein's words had an immediate effect.

18
00:01:23.269 --> 00:01:25.858
Heidi turned pale with fear.

19
00:01:25.859 --> 00:01:28.428
The book was Heidi's one treasure.

20
00:01:28.429 --> 00:01:31.894
She quickly dried her eyes and swallowed her sobs.

21
00:01:31.895 --> 00:01:38.733
Heidi never let herself cry out loud again, but she often had to struggle to keep back her tears.

22
00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:44.159
As the weeks passed, Heidi battled silently with her terrible homesickness.

23
00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.630
She would sit in a corner of her lonely room until Clara sent for her.

24
00:01:48.631 --> 00:01:52.914
She lost her appetite and did not know if it was winter or summer.

25
00:01:52.915 --> 00:01:58.670
Heidi began to look so pale and thin that Sebastian became concerned.

26
00:01:58.671 --> 00:02:02.228
One day, something very mysterious started to happen.

27
00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:05.751
Every morning, the front door was found wide open.

28
00:02:05.752 --> 00:02:08.892
Fraulein could find no explanation for it.

29
00:02:08.893 --> 00:02:15.444
So one night, Sebastian and John, the stable boy, stayed up to watch the front door.

30
00:02:15.445 --> 00:02:22.089
During the night, both men fell asleep, but John suddenly awoke to see a white figure before him.

31
00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:25.657
He gave a cry of alarm and Sebastian woke up.

32
00:02:25.658 --> 00:02:27.042
"What's the matter?

33
00:02:27.043 --> 00:02:30.452
What did you see?" Sebastian asked.

34
00:02:30.453 --> 00:02:33.435
"A white figure standing on the stairs.

35
00:02:33.436 --> 00:02:37.486
It stood there a minute and disappeared," explained John.

36
00:02:37.487 --> 00:02:40.856
Sebastian felt his blood run cold.

37
00:02:40.857 --> 00:02:45.941
When Fraulein heard the story, she immediately wrote to Clara's father.

38
00:02:45.942 --> 00:02:54.453
When Herr Sesemann read her letter, he did not believe there was a ghost in his house, but he felt that he should investigate.

39
00:02:54.454 --> 00:02:57.204
Two days later, he arrived at the house.

40
00:02:57.205 --> 00:02:59.611
"And how is the ghost getting on?"

41
00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:03.073
asked Herr Sesemann upon seeing Fraulein.

42
00:03:03.074 --> 00:03:07.740
"It is no joke, I assure you," replied Fraulein.

43
00:03:07.741 --> 00:03:11.332
"You will not laugh tomorrow morning, Herr Sesemann."

44
00:03:11.333 --> 00:03:18.162
Clara's father decided to ask his good friend, Clara's doctor, to come and spend the evening.

45
00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:23.519
The doctor arrived punctually at nine o'clock, and together, they waited up for the ghost.

46
00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.135
At one o'clock, there was not a sound in the house.

47
00:03:27.136 --> 00:03:30.122
Then suddenly, the doctor lifted his finger.

48
00:03:30.123 --> 00:03:32.379
They both listened.

49
00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:37.975
They distinctly heard the bar on the door being pushed aside and the key turning in the lock.

50
00:03:37.976 --> 00:03:41.245
"Who is there?" thundered the doctor.

51
00:03:41.246 --> 00:03:45.061
The figure at the door turned and gave a little cry.

52
00:03:45.062 --> 00:03:51.234
There, standing before them in her white nightgown, was Heidi.

